From: LYW-30M development <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] DFS: skip known non-radar subchannels without a failure warning

A 160 MHz CAC notification can cover both non-DFS and DFS subchannels.
set_dfs_state_freq() already leaves non-radar channels unchanged and returns
zero, but falls through to the warning intended for an unknown frequency.
Return zero at the matching non-radar channel instead. Keep the state update,
return count and warning for genuinely unknown frequencies unchanged.

--- a/src/ap/dfs.c
+++ b/src/ap/dfs.c
@@ -681,5 +681,8 @@ static int set_dfs_state_freq(struct hostapd_iface *iface, int freq, u32 state)
 		chan = &iface->current_mode->channels[i];
 		if (chan->freq == freq) {
+			/* A wide channel can include non-DFS subchannels. */
+			if (!(chan->flag & HOSTAPD_CHAN_RADAR))
+				return 0;
 			if (chan->flag & HOSTAPD_CHAN_RADAR) {
 				chan->flag &= ~HOSTAPD_CHAN_DFS_MASK;
 				chan->flag |= state;
